c.execute('update units set source_quality_notes=? where screening_unit_id=?',('Complete 22-page apparatus/assembly instructions and A-G retained. Installation text says 26 mm while equipment/task descriptions say 26 cm. Printed Euler equations use the opposite cross-term signs from the usual right-handed body-axis convention; the given algebra still yields harmonic frequency magnitude when I1=I2 and torque is set to zero. Torque-free F.2 model is a stated idealization, not evidence that physical gravitational torque can be removed by choosing a frame. No measurements or prototype construction were performed by this screening.','raw::317'))
